================================================================================================================
B1  THE FRW BACKGROUND OF THE REPAIRED ACTION (minisuperspace, sympy)
================================================================================================================
    H^2 = 8*pi*G*rho_0/(3*a(t)**3) + Lambda/3 + lambda*Derivative(phibar(t), t)**2/3;  minus GR: lambda*Derivative(phibar(t), t)**2/3  (vanishes for phibar-dot = 0);  phi equation: lambda*(a(t)*Derivative(phibar(t), (t, 2)) + 3*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(phibar(t), t))*a(t)**2/(4*pi*G) = 0  =>  phibar-dot ~ a^-3
  [PASS] B1 THE FRW BACKGROUND IS GR: on FRW the chassis and J vanish identically (a_m = 0, no spatial gradient, J(0) = 0), the Friedmann equation is GR's plus the inertia's kination term (lambda/3) phibar-dot^2, which decays as a^-6 (d/dt(a^3 lambda phibar-dot) = 0); with the declared phibar-dot = 0 it is exactly GR, and a0 is absent: a0(z)/a0(0) = 1
         measured: H^2 - H^2_GR = lambda*Derivative(phibar(t), t)**2/3; phi-equation lambda*(a(t)*Derivative(phibar(t), (t, 2)) + 3*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(phibar(t), t))*a(t)**2/(4*pi*G); a0 / alpha_c in Friedmann: False
         reading:  phibar-dot = 0 is declared initial data (like the dark mass): a free constant of motion, set to zero

