B2  THE LINEAR FRW EQUATIONS, DERIVED FROM THE ACTION (FP2's D machinery, read-only reuse, + the new sector)
================================================================================================================
    [Phi  ] new-sector part: B_ch*k**2*a(t)*chik(t)
    [Psi  ] new-sector part: 0
    [B    ] new-sector part: 0
    [E    ] new-sector part: 0
    [pi   ] new-sector part: B_ch*k**2*(a(t)*Derivative(chik(t), t) + chik(t)*Derivative(a(t), t))
    [theta] new-sector part: 0
    [delta] new-sector part: 0
    [chi  ] new-sector part: -(-B_ch*k**2*Phik(t) + B_ch*k**2*Derivative(pik(t), t) - 2*C_ch*k**2*chik(t) + 4*lambda*a(t)**2*Derivative(chik(t), (t, 2)) + 12*lambda*a(t)*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(chik(t), t))*a(t)
    J_P2 around zero field: leading order e^3 (the quadratic action has no J part); zero-field tangent J'(0) = 0
    (5 s)
  [PASS] B2 THE LINEAR FRW EQUATIONS, DERIVED: J_P2 is O(eps^3) around the zero-field background with J'(0) = 0 (no infinite tangent: FP3's G1t door, verified), so the quadratic action carries the chassis and the inertia only; the new sector enters exactly three equations -- the lapse (B_ch k^2 a chi), the khronon (B_ch k^2 d(a chi)/dt) and phi's own (4 lambda a^3 (chi'' + 3H chi') = k^2 a [B_ch (Phi - pi') + 2 C_ch chi]) -- and leaves the Psi, B, E and dust equations GR + khronon
         measured: J order e^3; tangent 0; untouched equations True; touched True

================================================================================================================
B3  THE ZERO-FIELD LINEARISATION: the Minkowski block of the repaired action (unitary gauge, symbolic second variation)
================================================================================================================
    dL/dn   : 2*k**2*(A_n*alpha_c - A_phi*alpha_c*sigma + 2*A_phi*sigma - 2*A_psi)
    dL/dpsi : 2*I*(3*A_B*c_2*k**2*omega + 2*A_B*k**2*omega + 2*I*A_n*k**2 + 9*I*A_psi*c_2*omega**2 - 2*I*A_psi*k**2 + 6*I*A_psi*omega**2)
    dL/dB   : -2*k**2*(A_B*c_2*k**2 + 3*I*A_psi*c_2*omega + 2*I*A_psi*omega)
    dL/dS   : A_S*k**2
    dL/dphi : -2*(A_n*alpha_c*k**2*sigma - 2*A_n*k**2*sigma + 2*A_phi*C_phi*k**2 - A_phi*alpha_c*k**2*sigma**2 + 2*A_phi*k**2*sigma**2 - 2*A_phi*lambda*omega**2)
    det M = 64*k**6*(C_phi*alpha_c*c_2*k**4 + 3*C_phi*alpha_c*c_2*k**2*omega**2 + 2*C_phi*alpha_c*k**2*omega**2 - 2*C_phi*c_2*k**4 - alpha_c*c_2*k**2*lambda*omega**2 - 3*alpha_c*c_2*k**2*omega**2*sigma**2 - 3*alpha_c*c_2*lambda*omega**4 - 2*alpha_c*k**2*omega**2*sigma**2 - 2*alpha_c*lambda*omega**4 + 2*c_2*k**2*lambda*omega**2 + 6*c_2*k**2*omega**2*sigma**2 + 4*k**2*omega**2*sigma**2)
    zero field (C_phi = 0): omega^2/k^2 roots [0, -(alpha_c - 2)*(c_2*lambda + 3*c_2*sigma**2 + 2*sigma**2)/(alpha_c*lambda*(3*c_2 + 2))];  product of roots 0
    CONTROL naive chassis: product of the zero-field roots -c_2*sigma**2/(lambda*(3*c_2 + 2)) < 0 -> one growing mode, omega^2/k^2 ~ -alpha_c*c_2*sigma**2/(2*(c_2*lambda + 3*c_2*sigma**2 + 2*sigma**2)); with the filter the band is bounded: max rate sqrt(alpha_c/2 lambda_eff)/(sqrt(e) xi) -> e-fold 67287 yr at alpha_c = 3.2e-09, lambda = 1, c_2 = 7.29e-03, xi = 0.03 pc
